# Web app conventions (apps/web)

- App Router only. Pages are async Server Components that fetch via `lib/api.ts`;
  push interactivity into small Client Components.
- Filter/selection state lives in the URL (search params), not global state.
- Use the typed client in `lib/api.ts`; do not call `fetch` to the backend
  directly from pages/components.
- Shared parsing lives in `lib/search-params.ts`; shared domain defaults live in
  `lib/constants.ts`. Do not hard-code metric ids, provider ids, default years,
  or chart colors inline.
- Reuse shared components (e.g. `KpiCard`) instead of duplicating markup across
  pages. Keep components under ~300 lines.
- Wrap external URLs in `SafeExternalLink` / validate via `lib/safe-url.ts`.
- TypeScript is strict; do not introduce `any`.

# Exhaustive switch

In switch statements over discriminated unions or enums, use a `never` check in
the default case so newly added variants fail to compile until handled.
